    {
      "id": "eb11c1-1:example-5",
      "type": "worked_example",
      "lo": "eb11c1-1:objective-1",
      "source_page": 4,
      "quote": "When expanding (x – 2y)^6, the term x^4y^2 is:",
      "stem": "When expanding $(x-2y)^6$, the term $x^4y^2$ is:",
      "solution": [
        "Since the exponent of $x$ is 4 and the exponent of $-2y$ is 2, ${}_6C_2 \\times x^4 \\times (-2y)^2$",
        "$= \\frac{6\\times5}{2\\times1}\\times x^4\\times(-2y)^2 = 15\\times x^4\\times4\\times y^2 = 60x^4y^2$"
      ],
      "answer": "$60x^4y^2$",
      "solution_provenance": "book_worked",
      "misprints": [
        {
          "field": "solution[1]",
          "printed": "6×5 / 2×1",
          "intended": "6×5 / 2×1",
          "notes": "Value 15 is correct; no error"
        }
      ],
      "provenance": {
