    {
      "id": "eb11c1-1:explanation-1",
      "type": "worked_example",
      "lo": "eb11c1-1:objective-1",
      "source_page": 5,
      "quote": "In the expansion of (2x^2 – 3)^7, the term x^4 has exponent 2",
      "stem": "Find the coefficient of $x^4$ in the expansion of $(2x^2-3)^7$ (Warm Up 1): the term $x^4$ has exponent 2 for $2x^2$, and exponent $7-2=5$ for $-3$.",
      "solution": [
        "${}_7C_5\\,(2x^2)^2\\times(-3)^5$",
        "$=\\dfrac{7\\times6\\times5\\times4\\times3}{5\\times4\\times3\\times2\\times1}\\times4x^4\\times(-243)$",
        "$=-20412x^4$",
        "Therefore, the coefficient of $x^4$ is $-20412$"
      ],
      "answer": "$-20412$",
      "solution_provenance": "book_worked",
      "misprints": [
        {
          "field": "stem",
          "printed": "exponent 7 – 2 = 5 for –3 7C5 (2x^2)^2 × (–3)^5",
          "intended": "exponent 7 – 2 = 5 for –3, so the term is = 7C5 (2x^2)^2 × (–3)^5",
          "notes": "The '=' or punctuation before the first expression is missing; check against the page."
        }
      ],
      "notes": "Printed under 'Explanation' as the worked solution to Warm Up 1; the final answer is underlined in red.",
      "provenance": {
        "by": "runbook/book-record.workflow.js ext-v5, sonnet, 2026-10-21",
        "method": "page image"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "eb11c1-1:explanation-2",
      "type": "worked_example",
      "lo": "eb11c1-1:objective-2",
      "source_page": 5,
      "quote": "Expand using the Binomial Theorem.",
      "stem": "Expand using the Binomial Theorem: $(3x-2)^4$ (Warm Up 2).",
      "solution": [
        "$(3x-2)^4={}_4C_0\\times(3x)^4+{}_4C_1\\times(3x)^3\\times(-2)+{}_4C_2\\times(3x)^2\\times(-2)^2+{}_4C_3\\times3x\\times(-2)^3+{}_4C_4(-2)^4$",
        "$=1\\times(3x)^4+\\dfrac{4}{1}\\times(3x)^3\\times(-2)+\\dfrac{4\\times3}{2\\times1}\\times(3x)^2\\times(-2)^2+\\dfrac{4\\times3\\times2}{3\\times2\\times1}\\times3x\\times(-2)^3+1\\times(-2)^4$",
        "$=81x^4-216x^3+216x^2-96x+16$"
      ],
      "answer": "$81x^4-216x^3+216x^2-96x+16$",
